1
00:00:01,042 --> 00:00:03,625
[angry chatter]

2
00:00:03,708 --> 00:00:05,083
-[battle cry]
-Lloyd, look out!

3
00:00:05,167 --> 00:00:06,792
-[gasps]
-[yells]

4
00:00:06,875 --> 00:00:08,292
[shatters]

5
00:00:12,958 --> 00:00:15,750
The medical bots assured us
Lloyd's condition is stable,

6
00:00:15,833 --> 00:00:18,417
but he shows no signs
he will wake up from this coma.

7
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:21,958
He has to wake up!
We can't do this without him.

8
00:00:22,042 --> 00:00:25,125
Whatever fears he had about
being our Master in the games--

9
00:00:25,208 --> 00:00:26,500
[knock on door]

10
00:00:31,167 --> 00:00:35,583
Oh, I thought Lloyd
would be, uh... Sorry.

11
00:00:35,667 --> 00:00:38,875
We came to do the official
transfer of elemental powers.

12
00:00:38,958 --> 00:00:42,917
Lloyd is technically the victor
of that competition.

13
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:46,708
But I guess we can wait
until he's... better.

14
00:00:46,792 --> 00:00:49,833
Good news though, we expelled
that pain-in-the-butt Zeatrix!

15
00:00:49,917 --> 00:00:51,208
I can hear you.

16
00:00:51,292 --> 00:00:52,750
And not just
from this tournament,

17
00:00:52,833 --> 00:00:54,458
but from all
future tournaments.

18
00:00:54,542 --> 00:00:57,167
That's it?! After what she did?

19
00:00:57,250 --> 00:00:59,208
Come on, Roby,
you can do better than that.

20
00:00:59,292 --> 00:01:01,292
Or we can do worse.

21
00:01:01,375 --> 00:01:04,208
Listen to me. I-- I was
so caught up in winning,

22
00:01:04,292 --> 00:01:07,417
in proving my worth,
that I blanked out.

23
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:10,208
I just acted out of rage.

24
00:01:10,292 --> 00:01:11,417
Rage?

25
00:01:13,792 --> 00:01:16,167
[dings]

26
00:01:16,250 --> 00:01:18,792
Was that supposed
to be an apology?

27
00:01:18,875 --> 00:01:21,667
I don't know what your
Caregiver-bot taught you,

28
00:01:21,750 --> 00:01:24,250
but mine always said apologies
should have the words

29
00:01:24,333 --> 00:01:26,125
"I'm sorry" in them.

30
00:01:26,208 --> 00:01:28,875
You know what should be done
to you, Creep-atrix?

31
00:01:28,958 --> 00:01:30,708
You should be... tied up

32
00:01:30,792 --> 00:01:33,458
in front of, like,
a really delicious melon

33
00:01:33,542 --> 00:01:35,417
that you'll never
be able to reach.

34
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:38,625
No, no, you should be poked
you with a million sticks

35
00:01:38,708 --> 00:01:41,458
while playing songs you hate
on a loop, forever!

36
00:01:43,083 --> 00:01:44,792
Yah.

37
00:01:44,875 --> 00:01:47,625
You don't know who
you're messing with!

38
00:01:47,708 --> 00:01:50,417
♪ Lost in the unknown
So much to see ♪

39
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:53,375
♪ Together we will rise! ♪

40
00:01:53,458 --> 00:01:56,542
♪ We fight ♪

41
00:01:56,625 --> 00:01:59,750
♪ Be a ninja
For what's right! ♪

42
00:02:01,125 --> 00:02:02,625
[explosion]

43
00:02:02,708 --> 00:02:05,250
-[growling]
-Stop!

44
00:02:05,333 --> 00:02:07,375
There ' s no fighting
outside the arena!

45
00:02:07,458 --> 00:02:08,917
I keep telling you this!

46
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:11,500
-[vibrates]
-Ah! Tell that to her!

47
00:02:12,708 --> 00:02:14,583
[zapping]

48
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:17,250
Sorry, Zeatrix.

49
00:02:17,333 --> 00:02:19,042
Lose your fight,
lose your powers.

50
00:02:19,125 --> 00:02:20,667
Them's the rules!

51
00:02:20,750 --> 00:02:22,792
-[bots warble]
-[screams]

52
00:02:24,208 --> 00:02:25,625
Ah!

53
00:02:27,250 --> 00:02:30,042
I'm sorry about that.
If Lloyd wakes up--

54
00:02:30,125 --> 00:02:31,500
When Lloyd wakes up.

55
00:02:32,458 --> 00:02:33,958
When Lloyd wakes up,

56
00:02:34,042 --> 00:02:36,167
I'll transfer all
the powers to him.

57
00:02:36,250 --> 00:02:37,292
He earned them.

58
00:02:40,333 --> 00:02:43,333
Wyldfyre, you saw Roby was
still wearing those cufflinks

59
00:02:43,417 --> 00:02:44,583
I told you about?

60
00:02:44,667 --> 00:02:47,667
Yeah. They look so fire.

61
00:02:47,750 --> 00:02:49,875
No! I-- I mean, sure,
they are stylish,

62
00:02:49,958 --> 00:02:51,167
but that's not the point.

63
00:02:52,375 --> 00:02:54,042
Those cufflinks have
the same design

64
00:02:54,125 --> 00:02:55,542
that was on the wall
from where

65
00:02:55,625 --> 00:02:57,250
someone sent
those attacker bots.

66
00:02:57,333 --> 00:02:58,750
Roby can't be a suspect.

67
00:02:58,833 --> 00:03:01,958
Did you see how he
just saved me? Us.

68
00:03:02,042 --> 00:03:03,958
Just because
someone acts nice

69
00:03:04,042 --> 00:03:06,542
doesn't mean they aren't
capable of turning on you.

70
00:03:06,625 --> 00:03:08,125
But this is Roby.

71
00:03:08,208 --> 00:03:10,333
What about Zeatrix? Or Ras?

72
00:03:10,417 --> 00:03:12,333
They're way badder!

73
00:03:12,417 --> 00:03:14,500
They're still suspects,
sure,

74
00:03:14,583 --> 00:03:16,125
but the more I think about it,

75
00:03:16,208 --> 00:03:18,333
the more Roby could easily
be behind the attack

76
00:03:18,417 --> 00:03:19,917
on the Matriarch,

77
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:22,125
and the attacks
on the other players.

78
00:03:22,208 --> 00:03:24,125
I think you're
the wrongest kind of wrong,

79
00:03:24,208 --> 00:03:26,083
but if this means
I get to prove

80
00:03:26,167 --> 00:03:28,000
the stang-zoot
Roby's innocence,

81
00:03:28,083 --> 00:03:29,458
then sign me up.

82
00:03:29,542 --> 00:03:31,708
I can help too, Arin.

83
00:03:31,792 --> 00:03:33,708
Thanks, but no, thanks.

84
00:03:33,792 --> 00:03:35,750
I need Ninja I can trust.

85
00:03:39,750 --> 00:03:41,750
[Arin's Dad]
Remember, Dr. Arin,

86
00:03:41,833 --> 00:03:45,667
when trying to solve a mystery,
trust no one.

87
00:03:45,750 --> 00:03:49,750
Everyone is a suspect
until proven innocent.

88
00:03:50,750 --> 00:03:53,500
Including... you mother!

89
00:03:55,375 --> 00:03:57,375
[chuckles] You got me.

90
00:03:57,458 --> 00:04:00,750
[all laugh]

91
00:04:04,667 --> 00:04:06,750
You sure you don't want
to go to the games plaza

92
00:04:06,833 --> 00:04:08,167
to see Sora fight?

93
00:04:08,250 --> 00:04:09,500
Very sure.

94
00:04:09,583 --> 00:04:11,667
Now's the only time
we know Roby and Bleckt

95
00:04:11,750 --> 00:04:13,917
won't be around their office.

96
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:15,625
[gasps, grunts]

97
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:19,125
[buzzing]

98
00:04:19,208 --> 00:04:21,250
We don't have much
time 'til the game is over,

99
00:04:21,333 --> 00:04:22,667
so we gotta hurry.

100
00:04:28,083 --> 00:04:30,208
-[door rattles]
-Well, we tried.

101
00:04:30,292 --> 00:04:32,625
Guess you'll have to trust me
that Roby's innocent.

102
00:04:33,667 --> 00:04:36,750
Would an innocent man
lock his office door?

103
00:04:36,833 --> 00:04:39,625
Yeah. Normal people lock doors.

104
00:04:39,708 --> 00:04:42,417
I was raised by dragons
and even I know that.

105
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:44,042
Hmm...

106
00:04:45,583 --> 00:04:47,833
[grunts] Ugh!

107
00:04:47,917 --> 00:04:50,292
Lloyd was trying
to teach me Spinjitzu,

108
00:04:50,375 --> 00:04:52,667
but I just don't know
what's holding me back.

109
00:04:52,750 --> 00:04:55,000
There's no chance I'm
making it past the next level

110
00:04:55,083 --> 00:04:57,000
of the tournament without him.

111
00:04:57,083 --> 00:04:58,833
Yah! [sighs]

112
00:04:58,917 --> 00:05:00,750
[Roby]
And for our next match,

113
00:05:00,833 --> 00:05:03,458
she'll wreck you with tech...
you,

114
00:05:03,542 --> 00:05:05,917
and now a bunch of
other cool powers --

115
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:07,667
Sora!

116
00:05:07,750 --> 00:05:10,542
Versus the Quake Snake
ready to break--

117
00:05:10,625 --> 00:05:12,917
the competition!

118
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:14,292
Frak!

119
00:05:14,375 --> 00:05:18,667
[crowd cheering]

120
00:05:21,125 --> 00:05:24,125
Something's up with...
What's her name?

121
00:05:24,208 --> 00:05:25,875
Jordana. Yeah.

122
00:05:25,958 --> 00:05:27,667
One minute she's
asking me for help,

123
00:05:27,750 --> 00:05:29,833
the next, she's pretending
she doesn't know me.

124
00:05:29,917 --> 00:05:32,375
Given how I ignored her
when we were in school,

125
00:05:32,458 --> 00:05:34,167
I wouldn't want
to know me either.

126
00:05:34,250 --> 00:05:36,333
Maybe her and Arin
can become friends.

127
00:05:36,417 --> 00:05:37,708
Friends that hate me.

128
00:05:39,792 --> 00:05:42,500
-[grand music]
-[gears cranking]

129
00:05:48,833 --> 00:05:51,167
[Roby] First game today
is a spectacular,

130
00:05:51,250 --> 00:05:53,333
multi-platform fight!

131
00:05:55,958 --> 00:05:56,958
You know the rules:

132
00:05:57,042 --> 00:05:59,708
first to fall, first to lose!

133
00:06:02,750 --> 00:06:04,833
Is everybody ready?!

134
00:06:04,917 --> 00:06:07,500
[crowd cheering]

135
00:06:11,375 --> 00:06:13,667
-[grunting]
-[fireball whooshing]

136
00:06:13,750 --> 00:06:16,375
[both grunt with effort]

137
00:06:16,458 --> 00:06:17,708
Hah!

138
00:06:17,792 --> 00:06:20,833
[grunts] Uh!

139
00:06:22,042 --> 00:06:23,083
Hah!

140
00:06:24,292 --> 00:06:26,250
[grunts]

141
00:06:29,875 --> 00:06:32,833
[grunts] Hah!

142
00:06:34,375 --> 00:06:36,083
[grunts]

143
00:06:36,167 --> 00:06:38,083
[quietly] Use your balance.
Whoa!

144
00:06:39,500 --> 00:06:40,708
[grunts]

145
00:06:41,625 --> 00:06:42,667
Yah!

146
00:06:42,750 --> 00:06:44,333
[grunts]

147
00:06:44,417 --> 00:06:46,042
Uh!

148
00:06:49,583 --> 00:06:50,542
[rumbles]

149
00:06:50,625 --> 00:06:53,500
-[clangs]
-Aah!

150
00:06:53,583 --> 00:06:55,292
[grunts]

151
00:06:55,375 --> 00:06:58,292
What's someone like you doing
fighting for Ras?

152
00:06:58,375 --> 00:07:00,375
You Ninja got him all wrong!

153
00:07:00,458 --> 00:07:03,333
Sure, he's strict,
but he taught me lots. Hah!

154
00:07:03,417 --> 00:07:05,208
[both straining]

155
00:07:05,292 --> 00:07:07,167
[explosion]

156
00:07:07,250 --> 00:07:09,542
[crowd cheering]

157
00:07:13,458 --> 00:07:14,667
[attack yell]

158
00:07:14,750 --> 00:07:15,833
Whoa!

159
00:07:15,917 --> 00:07:19,083
[crowd cheering]

160
00:07:24,292 --> 00:07:25,625
[grunts]

161
00:07:25,708 --> 00:07:27,375
[gasps]

162
00:07:27,458 --> 00:07:30,250
[Arin] Those masks
will make you more powerful,

163
00:07:30,333 --> 00:07:33,208
but they corrupt you,
poison you.

164
00:07:33,292 --> 00:07:37,000
Ras only cares about power,
no matter what the cost.

165
00:07:38,125 --> 00:07:41,333
Do it! Do not disappoint me!

166
00:07:43,083 --> 00:07:44,167
[clangs]

167
00:07:46,583 --> 00:07:47,625
[snarls]

168
00:07:48,875 --> 00:07:51,458
[both grunting]

169
00:07:51,542 --> 00:07:53,583
-Hiyah!
-Ohh!

170
00:07:54,708 --> 00:07:55,833
Ah!

171
00:07:55,917 --> 00:07:57,333
[grunts]

172
00:07:57,417 --> 00:07:58,500
Yah!

173
00:07:58,583 --> 00:08:00,750
-[crowd cheering]
-Ugh!

174
00:08:00,833 --> 00:08:01,917
Aah!

175
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:03,208
Ugh.

176
00:08:03,292 --> 00:08:05,875
Sora is the winner!

177
00:08:05,958 --> 00:08:09,292
[crowd cheering]

178
00:08:11,958 --> 00:08:13,667
[whooshes]

179
00:08:17,042 --> 00:08:18,583
[whooshes]

180
00:08:20,583 --> 00:08:22,625
[rumbling]

181
00:08:26,583 --> 00:08:29,333
You outplayed me.
Congratulations.

182
00:08:29,417 --> 00:08:31,250
You were a worthy opponent.

183
00:08:31,958 --> 00:08:34,875
-Congratulations, Sora!
-You have more powers, Sora!

184
00:08:38,500 --> 00:08:40,750
You have failed me!

185
00:08:40,833 --> 00:08:43,417
It was a good fight.
A fair fight.

186
00:08:43,500 --> 00:08:46,042
I will not suffer disobedience!

187
00:08:46,125 --> 00:08:50,375
I offered you certain victory,
and you refused!

188
00:08:50,458 --> 00:08:51,542
Ugh.

189
00:08:53,500 --> 00:08:56,125
I never want you
in my sight again.

190
00:09:03,042 --> 00:09:05,333
What? Jordana? Oh, hey.

191
00:09:08,875 --> 00:09:11,917
Huh? An Imperium
math equation?

192
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:13,708
What does this mean?

193
00:09:15,375 --> 00:09:16,667
[metallic rattling]

194
00:09:24,417 --> 00:09:25,500
Uh--

195
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:30,708
Hey, heh, I was just
looking for you!

196
00:09:30,792 --> 00:09:33,292
By your office! But of course
you were at the games.

197
00:09:33,375 --> 00:09:35,042
That makes way more sense.

198
00:09:35,125 --> 00:09:38,083
Anyway, I just wanted
to tell you that...

199
00:09:39,333 --> 00:09:41,208
you're funny and cute
and I like that!

200
00:09:44,333 --> 00:09:46,000
And you're a snazzy dresser!

201
00:09:46,083 --> 00:09:48,667
Those cufflinks are fantastic!
Can I see them?

202
00:09:48,750 --> 00:09:51,292
Sure! I think
they're kinda basic, TBH,

203
00:09:51,375 --> 00:09:53,167
but Dad used to wear them
so Uncle Bleckt

204
00:09:53,250 --> 00:09:55,083
thought I should wear them
for my first Tournament.

205
00:09:55,167 --> 00:09:57,125
-Aww.
-Right?

206
00:09:57,208 --> 00:09:59,292
Who'd'a'thought
Bleckt'd be such a softie?

207
00:09:59,375 --> 00:10:01,542
He gave them to me
right before the first game,

208
00:10:01,625 --> 00:10:04,042
like for good luck.
As if I needed it.

209
00:10:04,125 --> 00:10:05,250
[dings]

210
00:10:07,792 --> 00:10:09,500
[bangs]

211
00:10:09,583 --> 00:10:12,250
So, Roby got those cufflinks
right before the first game--

212
00:10:12,333 --> 00:10:14,292
the morning after
the bot attack.

213
00:10:14,375 --> 00:10:16,875
Told ya he was too cool
and good-looking

214
00:10:16,958 --> 00:10:18,292
to have left the mark!

215
00:10:19,792 --> 00:10:21,083
[musical notes]

216
00:10:21,167 --> 00:10:23,125
You have to
trust the evidence, Arin.

217
00:10:23,208 --> 00:10:26,208
Even if it goes against
what you believe.

218
00:10:28,792 --> 00:10:31,417
Even if your Dad is being
a real sneak.

219
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:33,833
[laughs]

220
00:10:33,917 --> 00:10:35,167
Yeah, you're--

221
00:10:35,250 --> 00:10:36,667
Right! I'm right!

222
00:10:36,750 --> 00:10:38,667
-Feels good! Yeah!
-[door creaks]

223
00:10:38,750 --> 00:10:41,792
[chuckles]
We interrupting something?

224
00:10:41,875 --> 00:10:44,083
Uh, just... feeling good.

225
00:10:44,167 --> 00:10:46,458
Not because of you or anything.
[awkward chuckle]

226
00:10:46,542 --> 00:10:48,125
But not not because of you!

227
00:10:48,208 --> 00:10:50,375
You're great! We're fine!
No big deal! Bye!

228
00:10:50,458 --> 00:10:52,792
[chuckles]
That's the wrong way.

229
00:10:55,625 --> 00:10:58,167
Um... [clears throat]
it was good to see you too,

230
00:10:58,250 --> 00:11:00,167
Wyfy. [clicks tongue]

231
00:11:00,250 --> 00:11:03,083
[squeaks]

232
00:11:03,167 --> 00:11:06,458
And the Elemental Master
of Heat has zero chill.

233
00:11:06,542 --> 00:11:09,125
Why aren't you at the games?

234
00:11:09,208 --> 00:11:11,708
Even if you don't support
your teammates,

235
00:11:11,792 --> 00:11:14,583
have some respect
for the tournament.

236
00:11:14,667 --> 00:11:17,208
[gasps, coughs]

237
00:11:17,292 --> 00:11:18,875
Yeah, good point, okay!

238
00:11:18,958 --> 00:11:20,542
[door creaks]

239
00:11:24,333 --> 00:11:25,333
Bye, now!

240
00:11:25,417 --> 00:11:27,250
Way to go, Sneaky Boots!

241
00:11:27,333 --> 00:11:28,792
[mysterious music]

242
00:11:30,667 --> 00:11:34,125
Detective Arin and Dr. Wyldfyre
are on the case!

243
00:11:36,667 --> 00:11:38,083
-Hmm.
-[boings]

244
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:44,208
You finding anything?

245
00:11:44,292 --> 00:11:45,333
Nothing.

246
00:11:47,958 --> 00:11:49,458
What were you expecting?

247
00:11:49,542 --> 00:11:51,375
A notebook that says,
"I'm guilty?"

248
00:11:51,458 --> 00:11:53,667
The entrance to a secret lair?

249
00:11:55,167 --> 00:11:56,208
No?

250
00:11:58,083 --> 00:11:59,458
Yes?

251
00:12:00,542 --> 00:12:01,917
And what's this?

252
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:03,667
[gears cranking]

253
00:12:03,750 --> 00:12:06,333
[gasps] I didn't break it!
You broke it!

254
00:12:07,542 --> 00:12:09,292
Well, well, well!

255
00:12:09,375 --> 00:12:12,792
The entrance to a secret lair!
[chuckles]

256
00:12:12,875 --> 00:12:15,833
For the record,
I'm the one that found it.

257
00:12:15,917 --> 00:12:18,000
It was smart of Bleckt
to hide the room's access

258
00:12:18,083 --> 00:12:19,542
in this old thing.

259
00:12:19,625 --> 00:12:21,833
No way Roby was gonna touch
a rotary phone.

260
00:12:21,917 --> 00:12:24,375
I still don't know
what this is.

261
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:37,625
[gasps]

262
00:12:37,708 --> 00:12:41,083
Who would do this to
his beautiful, beautiful face?

263
00:12:41,167 --> 00:12:45,750
So, I'm getting the feeling
that Bleckt doesn't like Roby.

264
00:12:45,833 --> 00:12:47,250
That sounds like a motive.

265
00:12:48,542 --> 00:12:50,000
-[pops]
-Ah!

266
00:12:51,708 --> 00:12:53,167
Can we go now?

267
00:12:53,250 --> 00:12:55,125
This room is gonna
give me nightmares forever.

268
00:12:55,208 --> 00:12:57,458
How is this all tied
to the Matriarch horns?

269
00:12:57,542 --> 00:12:58,833
We need evidence.

270
00:13:01,917 --> 00:13:03,333
Is that evidence?

271
00:13:05,958 --> 00:13:07,750
[Arin]
"Meet with Ras."

272
00:13:07,833 --> 00:13:09,333
Sounds like evidence.

273
00:13:09,417 --> 00:13:11,042
But why would Bleckt
meet with Ras

274
00:13:11,125 --> 00:13:12,750
the day before the Tournament?

275
00:13:12,833 --> 00:13:14,625
And if it was a meeting
to commit a crime,

276
00:13:14,708 --> 00:13:17,667
which it obviously was,
why write about it?

277
00:13:17,750 --> 00:13:20,083
He is pretty fussy
with his boring stuff,

278
00:13:20,167 --> 00:13:21,833
like ledgers and rules.

279
00:13:21,917 --> 00:13:24,417
We need more answers.

280
00:13:34,583 --> 00:13:36,958
Arin! I've been waiting
for you.

281
00:13:38,458 --> 00:13:41,417
I need your help deciphering
this note Jordana gave me.

282
00:13:41,500 --> 00:13:43,292
Who's Jordana?

283
00:13:43,375 --> 00:13:45,208
Oh, that girl from Imperium?

284
00:13:45,292 --> 00:13:46,833
Doesn't she hate you?

285
00:13:46,917 --> 00:13:49,583
Something weird is
definitely going on with her.

286
00:13:49,667 --> 00:13:52,083
And this is an Imperium
math problem.

287
00:13:52,167 --> 00:13:53,667
Maybe it's a clue or something?

288
00:13:53,750 --> 00:13:55,833
You're the best
at solving mysteries.

289
00:13:55,917 --> 00:13:57,083
I guess...

290
00:13:57,167 --> 00:13:58,458
I figured out the math...

291
00:13:58,542 --> 00:13:59,792
for all the good it did me.

292
00:13:59,875 --> 00:14:03,708
It spells out the words
"Crown Mono Stereo."

293
00:14:03,792 --> 00:14:05,542
What could that mean?

294
00:14:05,625 --> 00:14:09,208
Crown... mono... stereo...

295
00:14:09,292 --> 00:14:13,083
Crown... uh, hat... head?

296
00:14:13,167 --> 00:14:16,792
Horns? Horns!
Maybe the dragon horns?

297
00:14:16,875 --> 00:14:20,125
Then, mono... one?

298
00:14:20,208 --> 00:14:24,542
Stereo... around... hmm.

299
00:14:24,625 --> 00:14:30,000
Mono... stereo... monostereo...

300
00:14:30,083 --> 00:14:33,333
Monastery?
Horns in the Monastery?

301
00:14:33,417 --> 00:14:34,792
Is Jordana trying to tell me

302
00:14:34,875 --> 00:14:36,917
the dragon horns
are in the Monastery?

303
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:40,333
Maybe? But why would they be
back in the Monastery?

304
00:14:40,417 --> 00:14:42,625
[Cole]
Not in our Monastery.

305
00:14:42,708 --> 00:14:44,292
I think I know
which one they're in.

306
00:14:44,375 --> 00:14:46,417
But are you sure
we trust what's-her-name?

307
00:14:46,500 --> 00:14:48,042
Not sure we have a choice.

308
00:14:52,250 --> 00:14:55,833
[rumbling]

309
00:15:01,542 --> 00:15:02,750
-[slices]
-[grunts]

310
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:05,083
[thuds]

311
00:15:05,167 --> 00:15:07,250
[Source Dragon growls]

312
00:15:07,333 --> 00:15:09,875
[fire whooshes]

313
00:15:13,125 --> 00:15:14,542
[whooshes]

314
00:15:14,625 --> 00:15:15,792
[explosion]

315
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:21,292
Motion Source Dragon...
thank you.

316
00:15:21,375 --> 00:15:26,250
Your visions are from exposure
to Source Dragon Energy.

317
00:15:26,333 --> 00:15:30,125
I can ward them off,
but they will be back.

318
00:15:30,208 --> 00:15:35,000
Being a Conduit, as you are,
is a grave responsibility.

319
00:15:35,083 --> 00:15:37,750
And a responsibility
I have failed.

320
00:15:37,833 --> 00:15:39,750
I've lost in the Tournament.

321
00:15:39,833 --> 00:15:43,917
A Source Dragon like myself
would not have come to you

322
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:46,958
if I did not believe
you could do this.

323
00:15:47,042 --> 00:15:48,958
But we still haven't discovered

324
00:15:49,042 --> 00:15:51,375
who's behind the attack
on the Arc Dragons,

325
00:15:51,458 --> 00:15:53,167
or who's threatening you.

326
00:15:53,250 --> 00:15:55,167
Which is exactly why

327
00:15:55,250 --> 00:15:57,417
you must get back
in the games,

328
00:15:57,500 --> 00:15:59,375
no matter what.

329
00:15:59,458 --> 00:16:02,042
Lloyd, you must win!

330
00:16:02,125 --> 00:16:06,458
[gasps, panting]

331
00:16:09,583 --> 00:16:11,750
[gears cranking]

332
00:16:11,833 --> 00:16:16,375
Good afternoon, everybody!

333
00:16:16,458 --> 00:16:18,917
[cheering]

334
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:20,875
"Woo" is right!

335
00:16:20,958 --> 00:16:23,750
The next game
is gonna be a spicy one.

336
00:16:23,833 --> 00:16:27,917
First up, he's mysterious and
his handshakes really hurt:

337
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:29,667
Nokt!

338
00:16:29,750 --> 00:16:33,708
Versus... he's lean, green,
and definitely not mean:

339
00:16:33,792 --> 00:16:35,208
Lloyd!

340
00:16:35,292 --> 00:16:39,500
[crowd murmuring]

341
00:16:39,583 --> 00:16:41,208
What is Roby trying to pull?

342
00:16:41,292 --> 00:16:42,958
He knows Lloyd
is still in a coma.

343
00:16:46,375 --> 00:16:49,042
[sighs]
The Tournament must go on.

344
00:16:49,125 --> 00:16:50,875
[crowd murmurs]

345
00:16:50,958 --> 00:16:53,708
[sighs]
With Lloyd not attending,

346
00:16:53,792 --> 00:16:55,958
I'm afraid I must
call the fight.

347
00:16:56,042 --> 00:16:58,083
And the victory goes to--

348
00:16:58,167 --> 00:16:59,625
Lloyd!

349
00:16:59,708 --> 00:17:02,958
[crowd cheering]

350
00:17:03,042 --> 00:17:05,667
Lloyd! Come on, Lloyd!
You can do it!

351
00:17:05,750 --> 00:17:07,833
-Woo-woo-woo!
-Yes!

352
00:17:07,917 --> 00:17:10,958
Where are we go--
whoa...

353
00:17:11,042 --> 00:17:13,875
Looks like the orb that led me
here has made some friends.

354
00:17:13,958 --> 00:17:17,333
If you're right about
the Imperium girl's clue,

355
00:17:17,417 --> 00:17:18,833
this has gotta be the place.

356
00:17:18,917 --> 00:17:20,500
But how are we gonna
get over there?

357
00:17:20,583 --> 00:17:22,083
Our dragons were sent home.

358
00:17:22,167 --> 00:17:24,083
And you don't have your
Elemental Powers anymore

359
00:17:24,167 --> 00:17:26,292
-to make a bridge.
-Thanks for the reminder.

360
00:17:26,375 --> 00:17:28,250
And Sora's too busy fighting
to help us out

361
00:17:28,333 --> 00:17:29,875
by building us a ship
or something.

362
00:17:29,958 --> 00:17:31,708
Hey, I could come up
with a million ideas

363
00:17:31,792 --> 00:17:33,208
that won't work, too, like...

364
00:17:33,292 --> 00:17:35,292
Okay, I'm bad at improv

365
00:17:35,375 --> 00:17:37,500
but let's focus on trying
to come up with a plan

366
00:17:37,583 --> 00:17:39,500
that might work. Like-- ooh!

367
00:17:39,583 --> 00:17:41,625
I've got an idea!
Wait right here.

368
00:17:41,708 --> 00:17:43,208
Okay...

369
00:17:43,292 --> 00:17:45,500
-[flames whoosh]
-[upbeat music]

370
00:17:48,917 --> 00:17:50,958
What an unexpected comeback!

371
00:17:51,042 --> 00:17:53,042
Lloyd is back
in the Tournament!

372
00:17:53,125 --> 00:17:57,417
[cheering]

373
00:17:57,500 --> 00:18:00,833
This is so much cooler than
anything I could've planned.

374
00:18:00,917 --> 00:18:02,250
I'm not even mad you wouldn't

375
00:18:02,333 --> 00:18:03,750
let me use killer jellyfish
anymore.

376
00:18:03,833 --> 00:18:06,083
Lloyd! I'm so glad you're here,

377
00:18:06,167 --> 00:18:08,750
but you sure
you should be here?

378
00:18:08,833 --> 00:18:11,875
I can still fight. I have to.

379
00:18:12,792 --> 00:18:15,917
And here are the powers
that are rightfully yours!

380
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:18,583
[zaps]

381
00:18:18,667 --> 00:18:20,000
[dings]

382
00:18:21,833 --> 00:18:23,417
Lloyd, look out!

383
00:18:23,500 --> 00:18:25,583
[grunting]

384
00:18:26,792 --> 00:18:28,042
Yah!

385
00:18:28,125 --> 00:18:30,625
Ah... [grunts]

386
00:18:30,708 --> 00:18:32,625
-[grunts]
-Ah!

387
00:18:36,042 --> 00:18:37,958
-[zaps]
-[grunts]

388
00:18:38,042 --> 00:18:39,292
[grunts]

389
00:18:39,375 --> 00:18:41,292
Uhn!

390
00:18:41,375 --> 00:18:42,833
Ah!

391
00:18:42,917 --> 00:18:46,167
[cheering]

392
00:18:46,250 --> 00:18:47,333
[thuds]

393
00:18:48,542 --> 00:18:51,000
[Source Dragon]
Lloyd, you must win!

394
00:18:52,500 --> 00:18:53,958
[Lloyd grunts]

395
00:18:56,333 --> 00:18:58,042
[attack yell]

396
00:18:58,125 --> 00:19:01,542
Ugh! [panting]

397
00:19:03,208 --> 00:19:04,917
[grunts]

398
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:07,500
-[dings]
-Stop the fight!

399
00:19:07,583 --> 00:19:09,000
[crowd gasps]

400
00:19:09,083 --> 00:19:12,333
[panting] What?! Why?

401
00:19:12,417 --> 00:19:15,542
You are clearly
an injured combatant!

402
00:19:15,625 --> 00:19:17,958
According to ancient rulings,
the Source Dragons,

403
00:19:18,042 --> 00:19:23,417
in their desire for fairness,
do not permit injured fighters.

404
00:19:23,500 --> 00:19:25,542
Oh. Wow.

405
00:19:25,625 --> 00:19:28,292
Well, if it's in the rule book,
I guess...

406
00:19:28,375 --> 00:19:30,542
But you saw me.
I could do it!

407
00:19:30,625 --> 00:19:33,000
I'm just a little sore,
no big deal!

408
00:19:33,083 --> 00:19:34,333
I...

409
00:19:34,417 --> 00:19:36,333
I don't have a choice, Lloyd.

410
00:19:36,417 --> 00:19:39,125
Even though that match
was awesome!

411
00:19:39,208 --> 00:19:41,542
Your health is
the most important thing.

412
00:19:41,625 --> 00:19:43,375
You did not look well
this morning,

413
00:19:43,458 --> 00:19:46,292
and you still don't,
to be honest. Sorry.

414
00:19:46,375 --> 00:19:49,625
And victor by default is...

415
00:19:49,708 --> 00:19:51,833
Nokt!

416
00:19:51,917 --> 00:19:53,083
[gasps]

417
00:19:55,625 --> 00:19:57,000
[mysterious music]

418
00:20:01,375 --> 00:20:03,792
Well, hello there.

419
00:20:03,875 --> 00:20:08,833
[zaps]

420
00:20:11,250 --> 00:20:12,917
I'm glad you're awake, Lloyd.

421
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:15,958
I hope... I hope
you'll be okay.

422
00:20:19,500 --> 00:20:22,000
The odds were not
in our favor.

423
00:20:22,083 --> 00:20:23,792
You did your best.

424
00:20:23,875 --> 00:20:26,500
It wasn't good enough.
I've failed us.

425
00:20:26,583 --> 00:20:28,083
I've failed all of us!

426
00:20:28,167 --> 00:20:29,667
No, you haven't.

427
00:20:29,750 --> 00:20:31,000
I'm still in the games,

428
00:20:31,083 --> 00:20:32,625
I just need you to train me.

429
00:20:35,208 --> 00:20:36,250
[thuds]

430
00:20:36,333 --> 00:20:38,000
Cole, is that you?

431
00:20:39,542 --> 00:20:41,375
But that's
an elemental earth mech,

432
00:20:41,458 --> 00:20:43,958
you don't have your powers.
How can you get it to work?

433
00:20:44,042 --> 00:20:46,250
I'm pretty sure this mech
was my mother's.

434
00:20:46,333 --> 00:20:49,042
I can feel something in it,
some connection.

435
00:20:49,125 --> 00:20:51,625
So, maybe if I focus...

436
00:20:55,917 --> 00:20:58,250
[powers up]

437
00:21:02,958 --> 00:21:04,000
[thuds]

438
00:21:05,917 --> 00:21:08,250
[rumbling]

439
00:21:12,125 --> 00:21:13,167
[grunts]

440
00:21:18,083 --> 00:21:20,083
All right! Let's go!

441
00:21:37,417 --> 00:21:39,042
[mysterious music]

442
00:21:41,042 --> 00:21:42,250
[Cole]
Master Wu?

443
00:21:45,250 --> 00:21:47,542
[closing theme playing]

